# Witness: two exclusion sections in one bundle

Both sections below define the same exclusion, so nothing is undefined and nothing is
laundered. What is wrong is that a definition scanner reading the first match has no way to
know which of the two a reader would take as the bundle's exclusions.

## 9. Exclusions

| ID | Status | Exclusion |
|---|---|---|
| EX-01 | Open | The inbound half of the legacy-boundary rule is environment-conditional. |

## 9. Exclusions (superseded, kept for history)

| ID | Status | Exclusion |
|---|---|---|
| EX-01 | Open | The inbound half of the legacy-boundary rule is environment-conditional. |
